verses.text:
If they say, “Come along with us,
let us lie in wait for blood,
let us ambush the innocent for no reason;

Turn around at my reproof!
See, I will let my spirit gush out to you;
I will teach you my words.

Do not let loyal love and faithfulness leave you;
tie them around your neck;
write them on the tablet of your heart.

he taught me and said to me,
“Let your heart hold fast to my words;
keep my commands and live.

a loving doe, a graceful mountain goat.
Let her breasts satisfy you at all times;
be intoxicated always with her love.

When you walk, it will lead you;
when you lie down, it will watch over you;
when you wake, it will talk with you.

All at once he follows her,
like an ox going to the slaughter,
like a fool to the stocks for punishment,{d}

then I was at his side as a master craftsman,{g}
and I was his joy every day,
laughing and playing in his presence always,

The proverbs of Solomon.{a}
A wise son makes his father glad,
but a foolish son is his mother’s sorrow.

All the brothers of a poor man hate him;
how much more do his friends keep away from him!
He chases after them with words, but they are gone.{a}
